# Authors: Sunni (Sir) Morningstar & Cael Devo
# The question form asks what the statement form says; "not" flips it; what was never told is not known.
[before]
Does Devlin like rain? => !likes rain
[after]
Does Devlin like rain? => devlin likes rain
Does Devlin like snow? => devlin does not like snow
Does Marcus like snow? => marcus likes snow
Does Marcus like rain? => do not know
[after-correction]
Does Devlin like snow? => devlin likes snow ;; !not like
Does Devlin like rain? => devlin likes rain
Does Marcus like snow? => marcus likes snow
